      {
        "content": "There are 48 crayons in the box.  Kiley takes 1/4 of them away.  Joe takes away half of the remaining crayons, how many crayons are left?",
        "role": "user"
      },
      {
        "content": "24",
        "role": "assistant"
      },
      {
        "content": "Given:\n- Total crayons: 48\n- Kiley takes 1/4 of them away\n- Joe takes away half of the remaining crayons\n- We need to find how many crayons are left\n\nFirst, calculate how many crayons Kiley takes:\n\\[ \\frac{1}{4} \\times 48 = 12 \\]\nSo, Kiley takes 12 crayons.\n\nNext, calculate the remaining crayons after Kiley takes her share:\n\\[ 48 - 12 = 36 \\]\n\nThen, Joe takes half of the remaining crayons:\n\\[ \\frac{1}{2} \\times 36 = 18 \\]\nSo, Joe takes 18 crayons.\n\nFinally, calculate the remaining crayons after Joe takes his share:\n\\[ 36 - 18 = 18 \\]\n\nThe number of crayons left is 18.\n\nFINAL: 18",
        "role": "assistant"
      },
      {
        "content": "Write your own reusable record: explain the specific operations, when they apply, and a concrete check using this problem. Retain its final answer. Solve in your own first-person voice, using 150–400 tokens. Identify the given quantities and requested unknown, explain the actual reusable operations connecting them, and check the result against the problem. Do not pad with generic advice or invent observations. Finish with a separate line FINAL: followed by just the numeric answer.",
        "role": "user"
      }
    ],
    "prompt_tokens": 381,
    "raw": "Given quantities:\n- Total crayons: 48\n- Kiley takes 1/4 of them away\n- Joe takes away half of the remaining crayons\n- Unknown: Number of crayons left\n\nOperations:\n1. Calculate the number of crayons Kiley takes.\n2. Subtract the crayons Kiley takes from the total to find the remaining crayons.\n3. Calculate the number of crayons Joe takes.\n4. Subtract the crayons Joe takes from the remaining crayons to find the final number left.\n\nStep-by-step solution:\n1. Kiley takes 1/4 of 48 crayons:\n   \\[ \\frac{1}{4} \\times 48 = 12 \\]\n2. Subtract the crayons Kiley takes from the total:\n   \\[ 48 - 12 = 36 \\]\n3. Joe takes half of the remaining 36 crayons:\n   \\[ \\frac{1}{2} \\times 36 = 18 \\]\n4. Subtract the crayons Joe takes from the remaining crayons:\n   \\[ 36 - 18 = 18 \\]\n\nCheck:\n- Kiley takes 12 crayons, leaving 36.\n- Joe takes 18 crayons from the remaining 36, leaving 18.\n\nThus, the number of crayons left is 18.\n\nFINAL: 18",
